# JavaScript client discipline

Do not use `eval`, `new Function`, or string-built `setTimeout` handlers in
new or edited client code.

Keep typed boundaries: do not strip types or add `any` at module edges when the
surrounding files already use TypeScript.

Match the project's existing module format (ESM vs CommonJS) and path aliases.

Do not add a bundler, transpiler, or test runner the repository does not already
use. Extend the current toolchain instead.
